      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Finite-field and classical trace-like formulas linearize different objects. For a variety and regular map, graph-diagonal intersection becomes an alternating cohomological trace because the diagonal is the identity kernel; for classical zeta, logarithmic differentiation, contour residues, and Fourier test functions turn prime powers and zeros into dual distributions.",
