    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3cb9c17c5aa88f08f338d25c794e46b434c22f6a0e9a5fd3b7673370fd80c055",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Trace-formula family counts obtain their leading statistical mass from the identity orbit: in positive-volume harmonic families this becomes local Plancherel mass, paralleling the diagonal signal in the Petersson formula. A prescribed local condition of Plancherel measure zero removes that ordinary main-term resource, so standard limit-multiplicity machinery cannot isolate the constrained family before a zero-symmetry calculation can begin.",
