    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7177214385a4c33983a630f85653e04ebc8ef79a369d0ea58a7ce72f92c84993",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Correspondence algebra supplies a carrier for Frobenius-like operations but does not by itself control spectral size. The historical higher-genus program constructed the self-correspondence ring while leaving a norm or positive-definite form missing; later Weil-form and finite-field index mechanisms exhibit the additional positive-adjoint or sign structure that can turn correspondences into magnitude control, while the classical explicit-formula criterion leaves an analogous quantified sign burden unresolved.",
