    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_72feda41c955141b097c207cf1bfe9e5a3477b4cab772d0d75bc967ee329413d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For a nonreal Dirichlet character, multiplying the character and conjugate-character factors internalizes the conjugate functional equation in one analytic object whose divisor is the union of the two divisors. This representation-level self-symmetry is different from orthogonal or symplectic self-duality, where a pairing sign transported through conjectural motivic, l-adic, and automorphic realizations can obstruct central criticality.",
