      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_82cb48fc9bd2b245b4ebe29e98c059ef2eb396a393aa4ce17ca97aee9dcfeb92",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Both curve zeta functions and completed classical zeta display reflection symmetry, but the cited finite-field representation has additional finite spectral content: all extension-field point counts are compressed into a rational generating function with finitely many Frobenius inverse roots, and reciprocal-root pairing upgrades a one-sided radius bound to exact modulus q^(1/2). Classical completion exposes s↦1−s without supplying that point-count or Frobenius representation.",
