    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_86ae01eb9fc38d4c40ff3650b8466c9818b1a5876885b63b49ad7049137082b7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Automorphic trace formulas retain local representation-theoretic origin by pushing unramified Plancherel measure through an L-map to obtain Satake-parameter statistics. Random-matrix characteristic-polynomial models retain a different interface—family symmetry and conductor-scaled zero density—to predict universal moment structure, while the prime-local Euler-product contribution remains separate arithmetic data.",
