    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8bd4baf2986d3fc8c2c23acb8ff7b1e7c909c4e611577b5e4b805a88bb6723e4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For a modular newform, the period integral packages finitely many critical L-values as coefficients of a reciprocal period polynomial. In the stated large-weight regime, a normalized polynomial is compared with an exponential model whose unit-circle phase supplies alternating extrema, while a separate uniform error bound preserves the resulting sign changes and hence the circle-root conclusion.",
